Chapter: SerialLine
  cites Foreword chapter Board (UartConfig, default-uart-config)
  cites Foreword chapter Linear (freeze)

 A serial line HAL layered on the UART configuration in Board. Where
 the board UART drivers move raw bytes, this chapter models the line
 discipline that Modbus RTU and other fieldbus protocols ride on:
 RS232 (full-duplex, point to point), RS485 half-duplex (a shared
 two-wire bus where a driver-enable gates transmission), and RS485
 full-duplex (four-wire, separate transmit and receive pairs).

 The open port is a uniquely owned mutable resource: the type system
 forbids aliasing it (CDX2062), so the same line cannot be handed to
 two owners or used after it is passed on. On a half-duplex bus the
 driver-enable is itself a resource -- a linear grant that must be
 released exactly once (forgetting is CDX2063), so the bus is never
 left driven.

Section: Line Mode

  SerialMode =
    | ModeRs232
    | ModeRs485HalfDuplex
    | ModeRs485FullDuplex

Section: Line Direction

 On a half-duplex bus the line is either receiving (driver disabled,
 the safe idle state) or driving (driver enabled, transmitting).

  LineDirection =
    | DirReceive
    | DirDrive

  dir-is-drive : LineDirection -> Boolean
  dir-is-drive (dir) = when dir is DirDrive -> True is otherwise -> False

  dir-is-receive : LineDirection -> Boolean
  dir-is-receive (dir) = when dir is DirReceive -> True is otherwise -> False

Section: Configuration

  SerialLineConfig = record {
   uart : UartConfig,
   mode : SerialMode,
   de-active-high : Boolean
  }

  rs232-config : SerialLineConfig
  rs232-config = SerialLineConfig {
   uart = default-uart-config,
   mode = ModeRs232,
   de-active-high = True
  }

  rs485-half-config : SerialLineConfig
  rs485-half-config = SerialLineConfig {
   uart = default-uart-config,
   mode = ModeRs485HalfDuplex,
   de-active-high = True
  }

  rs485-full-config : SerialLineConfig
  rs485-full-config = SerialLineConfig {
   uart = default-uart-config,
   mode = ModeRs485FullDuplex,
   de-active-high = True
  }

Section: The Port Resource

 A port opens in the receive direction: on a shared bus a node must
 not drive the line until it explicitly enables its driver.

  mutable SerialPort = record {
   mode : SerialMode,
   direction : LineDirection,
   tx-bytes : Integer,
   rx-bytes : Integer,
   faults : Integer
  }

  serial-open : SerialLineConfig -> mutable SerialPort
  serial-open (cfg) =
   SerialPort {
    mode = cfg.mode,
    direction = DirReceive,
    tx-bytes = 0,
    rx-bytes = 0,
    faults = 0
   }

Section: Direction Control

  serial-drive-enable : mutable SerialPort -> mutable SerialPort
  serial-drive-enable (port) =
   port.direction = DirDrive
   port

  serial-drive-disable : mutable SerialPort -> mutable SerialPort
  serial-drive-disable (port) =
   port.direction = DirReceive
   port

Section: Discipline

 Transmitting is permitted whenever the line is not a half-duplex bus,
 or when the driver is enabled. Receiving is permitted whenever the
 line is not half-duplex, or when the driver is disabled. A transfer
 that violates the discipline is counted as a fault and moves no
 bytes, rather than corrupting a shared bus.

  serial-tx-allowed : SerialMode, LineDirection -> Boolean
  serial-tx-allowed (mode) (dir) =
   when mode
    is ModeRs485HalfDuplex -> dir-is-drive dir
    is otherwise -> True

  serial-rx-allowed : SerialMode, LineDirection -> Boolean
  serial-rx-allowed (mode) (dir) =
   when mode
    is ModeRs485HalfDuplex -> dir-is-receive dir
    is otherwise -> True

Section: Transfers

  serial-transmit : mutable SerialPort, List Integer -> mutable SerialPort
  serial-transmit (port) (bytes) =
   let allowed = serial-tx-allowed port.mode port.direction
   in let n = list-length bytes
   in port.tx-bytes = port.tx-bytes + (if allowed then n else 0)
   in port.faults = port.faults + (if allowed then 0 else 1)
   in port

  serial-receive : mutable SerialPort, Integer -> mutable SerialPort
  serial-receive (port) (count) =
   let allowed = serial-rx-allowed port.mode port.direction
   in port.rx-bytes = port.rx-bytes + (if allowed then count else 0)
   in port.faults = port.faults + (if allowed then 0 else 1)
   in port

Section: Queries

  serial-tx-bytes : mutable SerialPort -> Integer
  serial-tx-bytes (port) = port.tx-bytes

  serial-rx-bytes : mutable SerialPort -> Integer
  serial-rx-bytes (port) = port.rx-bytes

  serial-faults : mutable SerialPort -> Integer
  serial-faults (port) = port.faults

  serial-direction-code : mutable SerialPort -> Integer
  serial-direction-code (port) = when port.direction is DirDrive -> 1 is otherwise -> 0

  serial-close : mutable SerialPort -> Integer
  serial-close (port) = port.tx-bytes

Section: Bus Grant

 On a shared RS485 bus, permission to drive the line is a resource:
 acquire it before transmitting, thread it through each transmission,
 and release it exactly once so other nodes can take the bus. The
 grant is linear -- the compiler rejects a path that drops it (leaving
 the bus driven) or one that reuses it after release.

  serial-bus-acquire : Integer -> linear Integer
  serial-bus-acquire (node-id) = node-id

  serial-bus-transmit : linear Integer, List Integer -> linear Integer
  serial-bus-transmit (grant) (bytes) = grant

  serial-bus-release : linear Integer -> Integer
  serial-bus-release (grant) = freeze grant
